{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 34 (S4 L7-C, chapter 3): a boat pilgrim chain on open sea. Home isle west, rival isle east (a fortified harbor and a Hearth ringed by twenty posted wardens and eight towers), the high summit isle between them on the line of a sunken pilgrim road, the Tern and Storm isles close by and the Gull and Heron isles far to the north. Staged: raise a Boathouse; pray at the Tern, Gull and Heron Stones in order by boat. Each stone wakes the next, and its trigger lands that stone's guardians: unarmed rival pilgrims camped on its isle (settlers, so the level bot, which cannot clear armed guards on another landmass, can still out-pray them). Behind the player a rival boat lands a war band that kneels to pray the stone just taken away (raid pray, keepRaiders on). The Heron Stone lifts a reef path from the home coast to the Storm Stone (the level bot sends its boats with attack waves late in a game, so the fourth stone is reached on foot), and five posted rival wardens hold the Storm isle: the player fights through them on the reef. The Storm Stone lifts the pilgrim road: the player marches past the summit guards and burns the rival Boathouse in its fortified harbor (the rival may not rebuild one). Then the summit Reliquary wakes, a fourteen warden rival band comes over the road to pray it away, and six followers pray there for four minutes to finish. The rival AI sails its own pilgrims only from 1200 s. At 420 s a rival boat lands wardens on the Tern Stone: an idle player loses it (siteLost before stage 1). Bot stages near ticks 1050, 4000, 7200, 13900, 22300, 27750; bot win near tick 34200 (measured after S4 L8-A with the scenario Boathouse plan; unaided the bot places its own and wins near 29200).",
